hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1392","Yusuf bin Musa told us, Jarir told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: The sun was eclipsed. One day during the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, got up to pray, and he stood until he could barely bow, then he He bowed until he could barely raise his head, then he raised his head and could hardly prostrate, then he prostrated and could barely raise his head, so he started blowing. And he cries and says: “Lord, did you not promise me that you would not torture them while I was among them? Lord, did you not promise me that you would not torture them while we ask for your forgiveness?” When he prayed two rak'ahs, the sun rose, so he stood up and thanked God and praised Him, and said: “Indeed, the sun and the moon are two signs of God, so when they are set, be terrified.” To the remembrance of God.” Then he said: “Paradise has been offered to me, so much so that if I wanted, I could take some of its picking, and Hell was offered to me, so I made I blew it, and I was afraid that he would deceive you, so I started saying: Lord, did you not promise me that you would not torture them while I was among them? Lord, did you not promise me that you would not torture them? And are they asking for forgiveness? He said: I saw there the long black donkey with the kitten. She was holding her captive and did not feed her or feed her. You give it water and do not let it eat from the vermin of the earth. I saw it every time it turned around, it gnawed at it, and whenever it approached it, it gnawed at the fire, and I saw The owner of the two Sabbath prayers, a brother from Banu Da`ad, was pushed into the fire with a two-pronged stick, and I saw the owner of the shop in the fire who was robbing the pilgrim. With his socket, and he says: I do not steal, rather he steals the socket. So I saw him in the fire, leaning on his socket.”"
